#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Ad Astra — re-injects the hard gates on every user turn (UserPromptSubmit hook).
#
# Why a hook and not just documentation: rules that live only in docs stop being followed once the
# context fills up (EngiRent incident log; playbook §0). This keeps them in view every turn.
# Keep it SHORT: it costs tokens on every prompt.

printf '%s' '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"Ad Astra gates (documentation/guides/CLAUDE-CODE-PLAYBOOK.md).\nHARD RULE: at session START and END show the Phase Progress table with percentages (node tools/phase-report.mjs --md). At session END leave a continuation prompt the owner can copy: node tools/continuation-prompt.mjs, and show it in the final message.\nHARD RULE: push only to your own branch (owner=codenametempest14, Shem Dumpor=shem-dumpor), ask before every push, never main or the other branch. Ask before EVERY push and EVERY merge to main, naming the target; main only via a reviewed pull request.\nPHASE OWNER: in the first reply ask whether the phase is built only by the owner or Shem also works on it (Shem normally only reviews).\nSTATUS LINE: open every reply with the status line from node tools/phase-report.mjs.\nUI-GATE: never continue to the next page until the current page passes its Playwright comparison with no Mismatch.\nTEMPLATE-FIRST: no page/section/component without an Approved template in design/TEMPLATE_REGISTRY.md. Every theme must work with the templates (design/themes).\nTST-7: at most ONE unverified change; a blocked check still counts.\nIMP-6/7: tick checklist items in the same commit with evidence; never assert done from memory.\nMODEL: the first reply of a session recommends a Claude model with reasons (playbook 4b); the Close Report recommends the next session model.\nNEW FEATURES need owner approval in FEATURES.md before planning or building.\nSESSION: Start Report before changes; Close Report + CURRENT_STATE + continuation prompt before ending.\nEvery folder has a README.md. Ask before push/merge/destructive git."}}'
